# What `gcloud run deploy --source .` uploads to Cloud Build.
#
# This file must exist. Without it gcloud generates one from .gitignore,
# which does not cover the private directories kept in .git/info/exclude,
# and they would be uploaded.
#
# Default-deny: nothing is uploaded unless it is named here. That way a new
# private file alongside this repository is never sent by accident, and no
# private path has to be named in this public file.
#
# The rules use .gitignore syntax, which is not the syntax .dockerignore
# uses: here `*` would match at every depth, so the exclusion is anchored to
# the top level with `/*`. Without the anchor, re-including `templates/`
# would still leave every file inside it excluded.
/*

# The application
!/server.py
!/config.py
!/security.py
!/content.py
!/blog.py
!/search.py

# Dependencies, templates, static assets, and the articles
!/requirements.txt
!/templates/
!/assets/
!/content/

# Build instructions. Cloud Build needs these; the image does not.
!/Dockerfile
!/.dockerignore
